# Scrumban Rationale

I decided to use Scrumban because combining Scrum and Kanban allows me to organize the project in a way that is manageable for individual development.

Scrum helps me work toward broader goals through defined sprints, while Kanban allows me to divide that work into smaller and more accessible tasks.

Using a Kanban board also helps me visualize the workflow and track the progress of each task through stages such as Todo, In Progress, and Done.

This approach allows me to treat a large project as a set of smaller, relatively independent pieces of work, helping me maintain focus and clearly see my progress throughout development.
